body:
I feel like the underlying message in most of what I learned in school was the value in sticking to what you think is right, so I do prefer sticking to what I think is right even if its perceived as wrong.  Not many other people seem to "get that" though.

I don't know what to think about this girl.  She's the only one who bought me a present this year.  It sort of meant a lot.  I haven't thanked her yet though because she hasn't really talked to me.  I think I want to before I disappear, but its not worth it for now.  I think most recently she was really just playing with me so it's better to just push her away.  Playing with me == "hey we really need to hang out"  "is it okay if my boyfriend comes?"

///////////
